#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
rh-mcp — Robinhood MCP proxy with integrated OAuth (single-file, stdlib only)

Bridges MCP clients (ZCode, Claude Code, Cursor, etc.) to Robinhood's
OAuth-protected MCP server. Most MCP clients don't initiate the OAuth 2.1 flow
when an upstream returns 401; this tool holds the tokens and refreshes them
automatically, so once you run `login` you never think about auth again.

Architecture:
    MCP client ──stdio(NDJSON)──► rh-mcp serve ──http(+Bearer)──► Robinhood MCP
                                         │
                                         └─ on 401: refresh token, retry;
                                            if no refresh token: prompt to login

Subcommands:
    rh-mcp serve      Long-running stdio proxy (spawned by your MCP client)
    rh-mcp login      Browser PKCE OAuth flow (run once in your terminal)
    rh-mcp status     Show token validity and client config wiring
    rh-mcp self-test  Verify PKCE/SSE/config internals

Requirements: Python 3.9+ standard library only. No pip installs.

Config entry for your MCP client (ZCode example):
    "robinhood": {"type": "stdio", "command": "/path/to/rh-mcp", "args": ["serve"]}
"""

